  (text "OpenMUPP v1 AVR high-voltage adapter (adapter ID slot 8, R1 = 39k 1 %)\nTargets: ATtiny HVSP (J2, J3), TPI with 12 V on RESET, UPDI with the HV pulse on RESET (J4).\n\nJ1 plugs directly onto J4 of the OpenMUPP v1 probe. Pin numbers of J1 are the J4 pin numbers.\nJ4 pin 2 (reserved) stays open. J4 pin 16 (adapter ID) never goes to the target.\nPut only one target in J2, J3 or J4 at a time. HVSP: the probe supplies 5 V on VTREF.\nReset circuit (RESET_HV): reset = AUX2 high (Q1 on, 0 V). Run = AUX2 low, VPP off (VTREF through R2).\nProgram = AUX2 low, VPP on. R2 holds RESET at 0 V while VTREF is 0 V (HVSP entry needs this).\nFIRMWARE: never set AUX2 high while VPP is on. Q1 then shorts VPP to GND (current limit about 17 mA).\nR4 to R7 hold the HVSP Prog_enable pins at 0 during entry (J4 pin 8 is an input only, so SDO needs R4).\n     Not in the adapter plan. Check the pins against the ATtiny datasheets before layout.\nJ4 pin 1 (TPIDATA / UPDI) goes directly to J4 pin 4 of the probe. NO HV on the UPDI pin:\n     the ESD diode on J4 pin 4 clamps at about 6 V. The protection part for that is not designed yet.\nJ5 debug UART: labels are from the probe side (RX = probe input)."
    (at 30.48 45.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "193ea94c-7d7c-462e-92c9-059e69c33ab2")
  )
